#!/usr/bin/env ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

# Cross-demo copy check.
#
# The eight demos are eight standalone Rails apps, so shared application code is
# not shared at all — it is HAND-COPIED, and a set of copies that agrees today is
# a STATE rather than a check. So this script derives every relative path that
# exists in two or more demos and fails when a copy disagrees with its siblings in
# a way nobody declared: a new copy cannot appear silently, and a one-sided edit
# cannot land quietly.
#
# Every such path must appear in the COPIES manifest below with a rule and a
# reason:
#
#   :identical — byte-for-byte in every demo that ships it.
#   :code      — identical once comments and whitespace are normalised away, so
#                each copy's header prose may name its own demo. Ripper does the
#                stripping, so a `#` inside a string or a regex is not a comment.
#                MAGIC comments are the exception and are compared: they are the
#                one kind of comment that changes how the file RUNS.
#   :per_demo  — a genuine per-demo implementation that shares only a filename.
#                The FILE is not compared, and the entry records WHY the copies
#                differ. Individual methods and constants inside it may still be
#                held in lockstep — see the fragment rule below — and any SUBSET
#                of the copies that agrees once normalised must be declared in the
#                entry's `agree:` map, as `:lockstep` (one artefact, hand-copied,
#                and then held) or `:coincidence` (unrelated reasons, capped).
#
# `ships:` names which demos are supposed to have the file at all: a demo that
# ships it and is not listed FAILS, and a listed demo that does not ship it FAILS
# too. Entries without `ships:` are unconstrained.
#
# `except:` is the escape hatch for one copy that legitimately differs from its
# siblings. It is a demo => reason map, and it is checked too: an exception for a
# demo that no longer ships the file, or whose copy has since converged on its
# siblings, is an error.
#
# TWO AXES THE PATH RULE CANNOT SEE, and the manifests that close them:
#
#   * The db/migrate copies are `rails g kiosk:install` output, so all seven
#     operator demos can drift from the ENGINE together while still agreeing with
#     each other. Every install-generator template is declared in
#     GENERATOR_TEMPLATES, rendered with the generator's own default options, and
#     the render must byte-match the copy in every one of the seven.
#   * A HAND-WRITTEN migration that ships in two demos at demo-specific
#     timestamps is a singleton path that no template renders, so neither rule
#     above can reach it. Those basenames are declared in MIGRATION_PAIRS and
#     compared across all their copies; an undeclared one fails.
#
# An entry is DELETED the day its extraction lands rather than kept as a
# memorial: a copy set promoted into the gem that owns the contract is no longer
# a copy set.
#
# Stdlib only (digest + ripper + erb), no bundle, no database.
#
# Usage:
#   bin/check-demo-copies          # check
#   bin/check-demo-copies --list   # print the manifests as tables
#   bin/check-demo-copies --self-test         # plant a break per invariant in a
#                                             # throwaway copy and prove each reddens
#   bin/check-demo-copies --self-test --list  # the coverage table, run nothing

require "digest"
require "erb"
require "open3"
require "ripper"

ROOT = File.expand_path("..", __dir__)

# ── --self-test: one planted break per invariant, in a throwaway copy ────────
#
# This script holds many independent invariants behind one exit code, so a bare
# run answers ONE question about all of them — is the tree clean today — and
# cannot answer the other one: does arm N still go RED on the break it was
# written for. At this many rules a single reverted regex takes one invariant out
# of service while the exit code stays 0.
#
# HOW IT RUNS. `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard` in ROOT, copied
# into throwaway trees under a mktmpdir; one is checked green as a BASELINE; then
# each arm plants its break in a tree, runs the COPY of this script from that
# tree's own `bin/`, asserts exit 1 AND asserts the output names the invariant,
# then restores each touched file from the pristine original and re-checksums it
# against ROOT — «restored» and «restored to something else» are
# indistinguishable without the digest. Nothing under ROOT is ever written. A
# plant whose needle no longer occurs is an arm FAILURE, never a pass.
#
# TWO KINDS OF ARM, declared per row, because they answer different questions:
#
#   :break   — a FAITHFUL MISTAKE: a one-sided edit, a copy appearing where no
#              `ships:` set expects it, an exception that has gone stale, a claim
#              a sweep dropped from one document. Some rows plant in the MANIFEST
#              rather than in the tree, because that is where those mistakes are
#              made.
#   :vacuity — the rule's own MECHANISM switched off in the copy of this script,
#              to prove the in-band vacuity guard watching that mechanism is
#              itself alive. NOTE THE POLARITY: for a rule that is a BAN, «the
#              pattern must match something» is backwards, because a ban whose
#              violations match nothing is the ban being obeyed. So these arms
#              switch off the MEASUREMENT and expect the declaration-liveness
#              guard to fire, never a violation count.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER, because an over-claimed self-test is worse than none:
# an arm proves its rule reddens on ONE break, not that the rule is correct; a
# `:vacuity` arm proves the guard fires when its counter reads zero, not that the
# counter tracks what its name says. Every section carrying an in-band vacuity
# guard must carry a `:vacuity` arm, and the run fails naming the section when one
# does not — that coverage is derived from this file's source, so a guard added
# later reads as UNPROVEN rather than as absent. The fixture is a copy of the
# WORKING tree, so a red bare run makes this red too, by design, and says so
# before it runs anything else.
if ARGV.include?("--self-test")
  require "fileutils"
  require "open3"
  require "rbconfig"
  require "tmpdir"

  SELF_TEST_PROBE_RB =
    "# frozen_string_literal: true\n\n# A shared helper two demos grew in the same wave.\n" \
    "class SelfTestProbe\n  def self.call = :ok\nend\n"

  # The K-1088 and K-1090 arms plant in ALL SEVEN copies at once: a one-sided plant
  # is caught by the lockstep rule and proves nothing about the ban.
  SELF_TEST_SEVEN = %w[atablefor getgrocery hoteling philslist skooti stylish tudu].freeze
  SELF_TEST_AC_PLANT = SELF_TEST_SEVEN.map do |d|
    [:edit, "kiosk-demo-#{d}/app/controllers/application_controller.rb",
     "endpoints, the catalog link and the modules this origin serves",
     "endpoints and the schema, query, run, pay endpoints"]
  end.freeze
  SELF_TEST_404_PLANT = SELF_TEST_SEVEN.map do |d|
    [:edit, "kiosk-demo-#{d}/public/404.html",
     "for the register/login endpoints, the catalog link and the modules this",
     "for the register/login, schema, query, run, pay endpoints and the modules this"]
  end.freeze

  # The whole FRAGMENT_EXCLUDED entry for one path, removed the way a session that
  # thought the note was stale would remove it.
  SELF_TEST_EXCLUSION_RE = /^  "script\/redteam_suite\.rb" =>\n(?:^ {4}".*\n)+/
  SELF_TEST_DSL_LINE     = "    dsl_names.each { |name| fragment_dsl_ids[\"\#{rel}\#\#{name}\"] = true }\n"

  # Banners that are DATA or a HELPER rather than an invariant. The coverage table
  # is `every banner in this file` MINUS this list, so a rule added later appears
  # as UNCOVERED instead of not appearing at all, and an arm naming a banner that
  # no longer exists is an error rather than a silent no-op.
  SELF_TEST_NOT_A_RULE = [
    "--self-test: one planted break per invariant, in a throwaway copy",
    "The manifest",
    "What is NOT compared, and why (K-629)",
    "The engine side of the generator output (K-640, hardened at K-646)",
    "Cross-demo singleton pairs (K-648)",
    "Normalisation",
    "Magic comments (K-628)",
    "Discovery",
    "The e2e harness's fixtures, paired with the demo files they came from",
  ].freeze

  # ── T-155: THE IN-BAND VACUITY GUARDS, AND WHICH OF THEM IS PROVEN ────────
  #
  # A `:vacuity` arm proves that ONE in-band guard fires, so the coverage question
  # is asked of the SOURCE: a rule's section is "guarded" when it raises an error
  # whose own words say a MEASUREMENT stopped measuring, and every guarded section
  # must carry a `:vacuity` arm.
  #
  # THIS IS A LEXICAL PROXY AND IT IS DECLARED AS ONE. No syntax distinguishes an
  # in-band vacuity guard from any other `errors <<`; what distinguishes it is what
  # its sentence says. So the vocabulary below is the instrument, its FLOOR is
  # asserted — a vocabulary that stopped matching would print the same clean
  # coverage as a fully-armed file — and the sections it reads wrongly are exempted
  # BY NAME, an exemption that reddens when it goes stale.
  SELF_TEST_VACUITY_VOCAB = Regexp.union(
    /stopped matching/i, /stops matching/i, /no longer match/i, /clean zero/i,
    /reads as coverage/i, /vacuou/i, /read 0 /i, /reads 0 /i, /came back empty/i,
    /matched nothing/i, /matches nothing/i, /holding nothing/i, /compares nothing/i,
    /has stopped/i, /no live subject/i, /means nothing/i, /switched off/i,
    /cannot read is not/i, /over an empty/i, /empty corpus/i, /did not check them/i,
    /stopped being/i, /reads exactly like/i, /no rule read/i, /inspects nothing/i
  )

  # Sections the vocabulary reads as guarded that are NOT: a per-item complaint
  # that happens to contain one of these phrases. Each must still be matched by
  # the proxy, or the exemption is stale and says so.
  SELF_TEST_VACUITY_PROXY_EXEMPT = {
    "The one comparison this whole file exists for" =>
      "its two hits are the stale-`except:` and misplaced-`agree:` complaints, which say a MAP " \
      "records nothing — a declaration being wrong, not a measurement having stopped",
    "The e2e fixture rule runs (T-118)" =>
      "its hit is the per-fixture `silently compares nothing` message, raised for ONE unpaired " \
      "fixture; the rule's corpus is E2E_FIXTURES itself, which cannot go empty without the " \
      "undeclared-entry arm firing first"
  }.freeze

  # The floor is the number of guarded sections measured when this was written.
  # It is a MEASUREMENT, not a target: it may rise freely, and a fall means
  # either a guard was deleted or the vocabulary above stopped reading one.
  SELF_TEST_VACUITY_FLOOR = 18

  # The one rule with no `# ── … ──` banner, declared so the check below can tell
  # «an arm for an unbannered rule» from «an arm for a banner that has moved».
  # Its position in the count is not written down: `--self-test --list` prints
  # the invariant total, derived from this file's banners plus this one line.
  SELF_TEST_UNBANNERED = ["every demo lockfile resolves for the SAME platforms (K-962)"].freeze

  # THE PLANT TABLE. `rule:` is the banner the arm aims at, verbatim, so coverage
  # is derived from this column. `ops:` are applied in order to one fixture tree
  # and undone from the pristine original afterwards; `expect:` must appear in the
  # planted run's output, and the run must exit 1.
  SELF_TEST_PLANTS = [
    { id: "code-copy-diverges", kind: :break,
      rule: "The one comparison this whole file exists for",
      what: "a rename reaches ONE of seven `:code` copies — 057196e's exact shape",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-philslist/script/equihash_register.rb", "equihash_solve", "solve_equihash"]],
      expect: /script\/equihash_register\.rb: declared :code — the copies must agree.+\[philslist\]/ },
    { id: "magic-comment-lost", kind: :break,
      rule: "The one comparison this whole file exists for",
      what: "one copy loses `# frozen_string_literal: true` — K-628's exact shape",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-stylish/app/controllers/application_controller.rb",
              "# frozen_string_literal: true\n", ""]],
      expect: /application_controller\.rb: declared :code — prose may differ per demo, MAGIC comments may not/ },
    { id: "ships-stray-copy", kind: :break,
      rule: "The one comparison this whole file exists for",
      what: "a copy reappears in a demo outside the entry's `ships:` set — K-860/K-883 undone",
      ops:  [[:copy, "kiosk-demo-atablefor/script/bound_assistant.rb",
              "kiosk-demo-hoteling/script/bound_assistant.rb"]],
      expect: /script\/bound_assistant\.rb: hoteling ships this file but is not in its declared `ships:` set/ },
    { id: "ships-copy-gone", kind: :break,
      rule: "The one comparison this whole file exists for",
      what: "a demo named in `ships:` stops shipping the file and the declaration is not moved",
      ops:  [[:delete, "kiosk-demo-stylish/script/bound_assistant.rb"]],
      expect: /script\/bound_assistant\.rb: `ships:` names stylish, which no longer ships/ },
    { id: "except-has-converged", kind: :break,
      rule: "The one comparison this whole file exists for",
      what: "the excepted copy converges on its siblings and the exception is left standing",
      ops:  [[:copy, "kiosk-demo-tudu/config/puma.rb",
              "kiosk-demo-prove/config/puma.rb"]],
      expect: /config\/puma\.rb: `except:` for prove is stale/ },

    { id: "e83-harness-half-moves-alone", kind: :break,
  rule: "THE §8.3 LOOP EXISTS TWICE, AND ONE COPY IS NOT A DEMO (T-156)",
  what: "the §8.3 loop is corrected in the harness and not in the demo copy — the one-sided " \
        "fix this pair exists to catch",
  ops:  [[:edit, "e2e/schema_conformance.rb", "if examples_checked >= 4", "if examples_checked >= 3"]],
  expect: %r{script/descriptor_examples\.rb ↔ e2e/schema_conformance\.rb §8\.3: the harness half has moved} },
{ id: "e83-demo-half-moves-alone", kind: :break,
  rule: "THE §8.3 LOOP EXISTS TWICE, AND ONE COPY IS NOT A DEMO (T-156)",
  what: "the same correction lands in all seven demo copies and not in the harness, so the " \
        "`:identical` rule above stays green and only this pair sees it",
  ops:  SELF_TEST_SEVEN.map { |d|
          [:edit, "kiosk-demo-#{d}/script/descriptor_examples.rb",
           "if checked >= minimum", "if checked >= minimum.to_i"]
        },
  expect: %r{script/descriptor_examples\.rb ↔ e2e/schema_conformance\.rb §8\.3: the demo half has moved} },
{ id: "vacuity-e83-harness-banner", kind: :vacuity,
  rule: "THE §8.3 LOOP EXISTS TWICE, AND ONE COPY IS NOT A DEMO (T-156)",
  what: "the banner pattern stops delimiting the harness half, so the pair digests nothing and " \
        "reads as a clean run",
  ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
          "E83_HARNESS_BEGIN  = /\\A# ── \\d+\\. §8\\.3 /",
          "E83_HARNESS_BEGIN  = /\\A# ── \\d+\\. §9\\.9 /"]],
  expect: %r{e2e/schema_conformance\.rb: no `§8\.3` section banner} },

{ id: "new-copy-undeclared", kind: :break,
      rule: "Undeclared and stale manifest entries",
      what: "a helper lands in two demos at once with no manifest entry — how six of these got here",
      ops:  [[:write, "kiosk-demo-tudu/app/services/self_test_probe.rb", SELF_TEST_PROBE_RB],
             [:write, "kiosk-demo-philslist/app/services/self_test_probe.rb", SELF_TEST_PROBE_RB]],
      expect: /app\/services\/self_test_probe\.rb: exists in 2 demos \(philslist, tudu\) but is not declared/ },
    { id: "entry-no-longer-duplicated", kind: :break,
      rule: "Undeclared and stale manifest entries",
      what: "a copy is deleted, leaving an entry that compares one file to itself",
      ops:  [[:delete, "kiosk-demo-getgrocery/app/services/bad_proof_counter.rb"]],
      expect: /app\/services\/bad_proof_counter\.rb: declared in bin\/check-demo-copies but only atablefor ships it/ },

    { id: "exclusion-no-longer-true", kind: :break,
      rule: "The recorded exclusion must stay true (K-629)",
      what: "a cleanup deletes an inert generator file from all but one demo and leaves the record",
      ops:  [[:delete, "kiosk-demo-philslist/config/initializers/cors.rb"],
             [:delete, "kiosk-demo-stylish/config/initializers/cors.rb"]],
      expect: /config\/initializers\/cors\.rb: recorded in SKELETON_NOT_COMPARED .+ but only 1 demo ships it/ },

    { id: "template-regenerated-alone", kind: :break,
      rule: "Template ↔ copy: the drift the lockstep rule cannot see (K-640)",
      what: "the engine's install template is edited and the demos are not regenerated",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-server/lib/generators/kiosk/install/templates/create_kiosk_schema.rb.tt",
              "  def up\n", "  def up\n    # engine-side change that never reached the demos\n"]],
      expect: /create_kiosk_schema\.rb\.tt: rendered with the generator's default options/ },
    { id: "template-undeclared", kind: :break,
      rule: "Template ↔ copy: the drift the lockstep rule cannot see (K-640)",
      what: "a new install-generator template appears with no GENERATOR_TEMPLATES entry",
      ops:  [[:write, "kiosk-server/lib/generators/kiosk/install/templates/create_kiosk_audit_log.rb.tt",
              "class CreateKioskAuditLog < ActiveRecord::Migration[8.0]\n  def change; end\nend\n"]],
      expect: /create_kiosk_audit_log\.rb\.tt: new install-generator template not declared/ },

    { id: "ledger-id-in-generator-template", kind: :break,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN A SHIPPED GENERATOR TEMPLATE (K-1298)",
      what: "a fix wave cites its own row in a template `kiosk:install` copies into a consumer's repo",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-server/lib/generators/kiosk/install/templates/initializer.rb.tt",
              "  # Column on `users` that holds the principal id. Default :id.",
              "  # Column on `users` that holds the principal id. Default :id (K-830)."]],
      expect: /initializer\.rb\.tt:\d+: a ledger id in a template the install generator WRITES INTO A/ },

    { id: "ledger-id-in-demo-code", kind: :break,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
      what: "an id lands in a `desc` body — what `rake -D` prints, K-1323's exact operator-facing shape",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-hoteling/lib/tasks/demo.rake",
              "DB-free unit spec for the WireArguments shape guards",
              "DB-free unit spec for the WireArguments shape guards (K-1099)"]],
      expect: /lib\/tasks\/demo\.rake:\d+: a ledger id OUTSIDE a comment, in code this demo RUNS/ },
    { id: "vacuity-demo-ledger-ids", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
      what: "the pattern stops matching a shape people write, so a BAN with a dead pattern must say so",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "  \"# The past-slot filter, K-480.\",\n", "  \"# The past-slot filter, 480.\",\n"]],
      expect: /the K-1383 ledger-id pattern no longer matches its own fixture/ },

    { id: "spec-harness-unit-drifts", kind: :break,
      rule: "THE DEMO SPEC HARNESS, HELD BY UNIT NAME RATHER THAN BY PATH (K-1536)",
      what: "one demo's copy of `guard` grows a rescue clause the other five do not have",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-tudu/spec/reader_clock_spec.rb",
              "def guard(label)\n  yield\nrescue StandardError => e",
              "def guard(label)\n  yield\nrescue StandardError, NameError => e"]],
      expect: /guard: the demo spec copies must agree once comments and whitespace are normalised/ },
    { id: "spec-harness-undeclared-unit", kind: :break,
      rule: "THE DEMO SPEC HARNESS, HELD BY UNIT NAME RATHER THAN BY PATH (K-1536)",
      what: "a helper is copied into a second demo's spec, at a path no other demo has",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-stylish/spec/salon_clock_spec.rb",
              "FAILURES = []", "FAILURES = []\n\ndef probe_shared_helper = :ok"],
             [:edit, "kiosk-demo-skooti/spec/licence_flag_spec.rb",
              "FAILURES = []", "FAILURES = []\n\ndef probe_shared_helper = :ok"]],
      expect: /probe_shared_helper: defined in 2 demo spec\/test file\(s\).*declared NOWHERE/ },
    { id: "spec-harness-undeclared-unit-half-path-keyed", kind: :break,
      rule: "THE DEMO SPEC HARNESS, HELD BY UNIT NAME RATHER THAN BY PATH (K-1536)",
      what: "the same helper lands in ONE copy of the shared path AND in a demo-unique spec — the " \
            "case the old justification said could not exist, and the message must COUNT the " \
            "reach of the path-keyed rule rather than claim it is zero",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-atablefor/spec/wire_arguments_spec.rb",
              "FAILURES = []", "FAILURES = []\n\ndef probe_reach_helper = :ok"],
             [:edit, "kiosk-demo-stylish/spec/salon_clock_spec.rb",
              "FAILURES = []", "FAILURES = []\n\ndef probe_reach_helper = :ok"]],
      expect: /probe_reach_helper: defined in 2 .*1 of them sits at a relative path FRAGMENTS walks and 1 does not/ },
    { id: "vacuity-spec-harness-corpus", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "THE DEMO SPEC HARNESS, HELD BY UNIT NAME RATHER THAN BY PATH (K-1536)",
      what: "the corpus glob stops matching, so a lockstep rule over nothing exits 0",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "DEMO_SPEC_SUBDIRS = %w[spec test].freeze",
              "DEMO_SPEC_SUBDIRS = %w[spec_gone].freeze"]],
      expect: /the demo-spec harness rule read 0 Ruby file\(s\)/ },
    { id: "spec-whole-file-copied-at-one-path", kind: :break,
      rule: "A SPEC PATH TWO DEMOS SHARE MUST REACH THE FILE MANIFEST (K-1550)",
      what: "a whole spec file copied into a second demo at the SAME relative path, whose every " \
            "unit name is ALREADY declared — so the name-keyed rule compares them, they agree, " \
            "and the file itself is held by nothing (measured: bare guard exit 0)",
      ops:  [[:copy, "kiosk-demo-philslist/spec/board_clock_spec.rb",
              "kiosk-demo-tudu/spec/board_clock_spec.rb"]],
      expect: %r{spec/board_clock_spec\.rb: 2 demos ship a file at this SAME relative path} },
    { id: "vacuity-spec-shared-path-key", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "A SPEC PATH TWO DEMOS SHARE MUST REACH THE FILE MANIFEST (K-1550)",
      what: "the group key keeps its demo directory, so every path is unique by construction and " \
            "no duplicate can ever be found",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "spec_by_relpath   = spec_corpus.group_by { |rel| rel.split(\"/\", 2).last }",
              "spec_by_relpath   = spec_corpus.group_by { |rel| rel }"]],
      expect: /the K-1550 shared-path rule grouped \d+ key\(s\) and \d+ of them are not a path/ },
    { id: "vacuity-spec-harness-stale-entry", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "THE DEMO SPEC HARNESS, HELD BY UNIT NAME RATHER THAN BY PATH (K-1536)",
      what: "a declared unit name that the corpus no longer shares reads as coverage",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "  \"at_dublin\" => {\n", "  \"at_dublin_renamed\" => {\n"]],
      expect: /SPEC_UNITS\["at_dublin_renamed"\]: declared, but it is defined in 0 file\(s\)/ },
    { id: "ledger-id-behind-an-escape", kind: :break,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
      what: "the id follows a `\\n` inside the string, so a leading `\\b` never matched it (K-1537)",
      ops:  [[:edit, "kiosk-demo-hoteling/lib/tasks/demo.rake",
              "desc \"DB-free unit spec for the WireArguments shape guards",
              "desc \"\\nK-1099 DB-free unit spec for the WireArguments shape guards"]],
      expect: /lib\/tasks\/demo\.rake:\d+: a ledger id OUTSIDE a comment, in code this demo RUNS/ },
    { id: "vacuity-demo-ledger-escape-blind", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
      what: "the leading boundary goes back to a bare `\\b`, which is blind to every escape (K-1537)",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "LEDGER_WORD_START      = \"(?:\#{LEDGER_ESCAPE_RUN_ALTS.join('|')}|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_]))\"\n",
              "LEDGER_WORD_START      = \"\\\\b\"\n"]],
      expect: /misses an id behind the escape\(s\)/ },
    { id: "vacuity-demo-ledger-boundary-dropped", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
      what: "the boundary is DELETED instead of taught about escapes, so `SK-001` becomes a ledger id",
      ops:  [[:edit, "bin/check-demo-copies",
              "LEDGER_WORD_START      = \"(?:\#{LEDGER_ESCAPE_RUN_ALTS.join('|')}|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_]))\"\n",
              "LEDGER_WORD_START      = \"\"\n"]],
      expect: /now matches a shape that is NOT a ledger id/ },
    { id: "vacuity-demo-ledger-lexer", kind: :vacuity,
      rule: "NO LEDGER ID IN CODE A DEMO RUNS (K-1383)",
