           "three. `dependent: nil` is the load-bearing half: the rows belong to the ENGINE, so a " \
           "copy that grows a `:destroy` would have a demo delete kiosk-server's settlement " \
           "records, and it would do it in one demo only.",
  },
  "app/models/cart_mandate.rb#scope" => {
    rule:  :per_demo,
    ships: %w[getgrocery hoteling skooti],
    why:   "SAME NAME, EACH DEMO'S OWN KEY: `scope :referencing` keys the jsonb containment on " \
           "`order_id`, `booking_id` and `reservation_id` respectively — the line item each " \
           "operator's settled cart actually names. The Arel node and the `@>` operator are " \
