           "declared so the association SET is under the discovery rule, which is what notices a " \
           "seventh demo growing one.",
  },
  "app/models/booking.rb#belongs_to" => {
    rule:  :per_demo,
    ships: %w[atablefor hoteling],
    why:   "SAME MACRO, EACH DEMO'S OWN PARENTS — `user`/`restaurant`/`restaurant_table` against " \
           "`user`/`property`/`room_type`. One unit rather than three (the head is the handle), " \
           "so what is compared is the whole association SET in file order: an association DROPPED " \
           "in one copy is the drift this rule exists for, and a per-association name would report " \
           "it as a unit that merely stopped being shared.",
  },
  "app/models/booking.rb#scope" => {
